---
name: task-refused
version: 1.0.0
description: Refusal report for any atm-bd-orchestration assignment that cannot be done at all; the body of `atm task close <task-id> refused`. States what happened to the bead so the lead can act.
format: markdown
required_variables:
  - generated_at
  - task_id
  - stage
  - bead_state
  - reason_md
optional_variables:
  - sprint
  - branch
  - commit
  - notes_md
defaults:
  sprint: ""
  branch: ""
  commit: ""
  notes_md: ""
metadata:
  type: task-refused
  tags:
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: refused
    stage: refused
    transition: complete
---
{% if bead_state not in ["open", "blocked-failed"] %}{{ bead_state | bead_state_must_be_open_or_blocked_failed }}ERROR: bead_state must be open or blocked-failed, got {{ bead_state }}
{% endif %}# Task Refused

Generated: {{ generated_at }}
Task/Bead: {{ task_id }} ({% if sprint %}sprint {{ sprint }}, {% endif %}stage {{ stage }})
Bead left: **{{ bead_state }}**
{% if branch %}Branch: `{{ branch }}`{% if commit %} at `{{ commit }}`{% endif %}
{% endif %}
## Machine Status (JSON)
```json
{
  "task": {{ task_id | tojson }},
  "sprint": {{ sprint | tojson }},
  "stage": {{ stage | tojson }},
  "bead_state": {{ bead_state | tojson }},
  "branch": {{ branch | tojson }},
  "commit": {{ commit | tojson }}
}
```

